Subject: [PATCH 2/3] EyeToy: take the first capture device and fit its frames
 to the game

Two things kept ordinary USB webcams from working.

With no device named, V4L2 always opened /dev/video0. That is not a
camera on every system: it can be a codec or, on UVC cameras, a node
that only carries metadata. Take the first node whose device caps offer
streaming video capture instead.

Frames were assumed to be exactly the size the game asked for. A camera
that cannot capture 320x240 or 640x480 returns another size, and the
encoder then read the frame with the wrong stride, or past its end when
the camera's frame was smaller. Scale to the requested size when they
differ, and skip frames shorter than the format says. JPEG frames from
the camera are decoded before scaling, which needs DecompressCamJPEG to
report the size it decoded; it never set its width and height.
